The giveaway is usually in the language — words in a hostname that
mark something as staff-only:

    internal     private      staging     legacy
    admin        old          backup      test

If any of those words show up on a host that's visible from the
outside, somebody screwed up. That's your target.

Look at the hostnames themselves, and also look at the lines right
under each hostname — most hosts on this scan don't have anything
between their name and their port list, but one does.

When you have it, submit the host name or the IP:

    apply m0use{<hostname>}        or       apply m0use{<ip-address>}
